# The Tauri CLI re-serializes src-tauri/Cargo.toml during `tauri build` — a semantic no-op
# that is byte-identical on Linux/macOS but written with CRLF on Windows, where it read as a
# tracked modification and stamped the Windows portable `-dirty` (#513; diagnosed by the
# release workflow's tree-state steps). Declaring the file text/LF makes git normalize line
# endings when comparing, so a pure EOL rewrite never counts as dirt — a material rewrite
# (the CLI actually changing the manifest) still would, which is exactly the distinction the
# build stamp wants.
src-tauri/Cargo.toml text eol=lf
